{
  "opening": "This release introduces several new functional composition and iteration utilities while refining existing dictionary operations. It also updates internal warning mechanisms and ensures compatibility with modern Python environments by dropping legacy support.",
  "requirements": [
    {
      "id": "m01",
      "text": "The public API must expose the `apply` function, which accepts a callable and arguments to invoke it. Additionally, `identity` and `thread_first` must be available for basic data transformation and piping."
    },
    {
      "id": "m02",
      "text": "The library must provide `compose_left`, `compose`, and `pipe` functions for chaining operations. These functions should accept callables and return a new callable that applies them in sequence."
    },
    {
      "id": "m03",
      "text": "The public API must include `peekn` and `peek` functions that allow inspecting values in a pipeline without altering the data flow. These functions should return the input value unchanged after performing an observation side effect."
    },
    {
      "id": "m07",
      "text": "The `fold` function must continue to support parallel reduction operations on iterables. Its signature and behavior regarding chunking and combining results should remain consistent with previous stable releases."
    },
    {
      "id": "m09",
      "text": "Any functions involving breakpoints or debugging signals must maintain their standard exception signatures. No changes to error types or traceback formats are required for this update."
    },
    {
      "id": "m14",
      "text": "The `merge` and `merge_with` functions must accept any object implementing the `Mapping` protocol, not just strict dictionaries. They should correctly combine key-value pairs from multiple mapping inputs."
    },
    {
      "id": "m18",
      "text": "All listed functions including `Compose`, `curry`, `excepts`, and others must operate exclusively under Python 3 syntax and semantics. Legacy Python 2 specific behaviors or imports must be completely removed from these public interfaces."
    },
    {
      "id": "m31",
      "text": "The `get_config_from_root` function must emit improved warnings when configuration issues are detected. These warnings should clearly indicate the nature of the configuration problem to aid debugging."
    }
  ],
  "closing": "Please ensure all public names are exported correctly and that the removal of Python 2 support does not introduce regressions for current users."
}
